From: priangle <203159732+priangle@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 19:39:25 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] crt-emu: pill sliders in the panel

The panel's sliders are a thin line with a pill-shaped handle that
carries the value, so the number is never hidden under the handle (the
stock ImGui grab sat over the centred value). The line is amber from
the start, or from zero when zero is inside the range, up to the pill;
the pill is as wide as the slider's widest value and keeps its size.
Input is ImGui's own, as in ImGui::SliderScalar (drag, Ctrl+click to
type, arrows); the pill is the grab rectangle SliderBehavior returns.
The magnifier's zoom and size are rows like the parameters.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015yjP4pBYqkzwik2NkFF1dK
